WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.900
In the final years of the Ming dynasty, the eunuch Wei Zhongxian held great power at court, and many officials had to watch his mood before acting.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.000
Wherever he passed, palace maids and eunuchs all bowed their heads in salute.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.100
Backed by his power at court, Wei Zhongxian grew more and more arrogant, surrounded by flatterers.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.300
Box after box of gifts was delivered to his rooms, piled up as high as a small hill.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:28.000
Wei Zhongxian pushed out the Donglin officials who opposed him, and the quarrels at court grew fiercer and fiercer.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.600
After the young Chongzhen Emperor took the throne, he resolved to clean up the court and never again let a eunuch hold unchecked power.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:42.400
The emperor ordered Wei Zhongxian's faction purged; the grand chair stood empty, and the palace gates slowly closed.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.700
The empty grand chair remained in the great hall, and no one dared go near it again.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.500
This chapter of history became a symbol of late-Ming corruption and factional strife, reminding later generations to remember its lesson.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.600
Sunlight shone into the quiet courtyard, and a new day brought new hope.
